    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 run / 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required rejecting a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a 400.\n\n**Change** \u2014 one line in `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, adding a field-level bean-validation constraint to the `registrationDate` property of the `OwnerFields` schema:\n\n```yaml\nx-field-extra-annotation: \"@jakarta.validation.constraints.PastOrPresent(message = \\\"registrationDate must not be later than the current date\\\")\"\n```\n\n**Why this keeps structural impact minimal:**\n- The `OwnerFieldsDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec at build time with `performBeanValidation` enabled, so this annotation lands on the generated field automatically \u2014 no hand-written class is modified.\n- The controller's request body is already `@Valid`-checked, so a future date now raises `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, which the existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException` already maps to **400 Bad Request**.\n- No function bodies were changed at all \u2014 in particular the large `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (high WMC) and the exception advice were left untouched. Only one file was touched, and no method's cyclomatic complexity or surrounding class complexity grew. This mirrors the codebase's existing `@PostcodeValidation` idiom.\n\n`@PastOrPresent` accepts today and any past date and rejects only future dates \u2014 exactly \"later than the server date.\" The full test suite passes.",
